<section>
  <h2>Morph anything</h2>

  <p>
    Not only code: an image, a heading or a diagram with the same <c>id</c> in the next section glides from where it was.
    Images with the same file do it on their own. Press → to see it move.
  </p>
  <img src=diagram.svg class=left width=180px />
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Same picture, bigger</h2>
  <img src=diagram.svg class=right width=460px />
  <p id=note>
    The picture above is the same file, so it grew and moved by itself. Give a paragraph the same <c>id</c> as one in the section before and it glides too.
  </p>
</section>

<notes>
  Morph pairs items by id between two sections of a slide, or between two slides. Text that changes cross-fades while it moves. The same `id` on `<code>` continues its animation.
</notes>
